      "module_name": "release_counter",
      "parent_id": null,
      "behavior": "Use clk_ctr and synchronous active-high rst_ctr; sample reset only at the rising clock edge. One elastic output slot and a modulo-16 counter. data_in is a 4-bit unsigned increment, data_in_valid enables a command, data_out_ready is output readiness. On reset data_out=0 and data_out_valid=0. Otherwise can_accept=(!old_data_out_valid)||data_out_ready; when can_accept, data_out_valid=data_in_valid and accepted command adds data_in modulo16 to data_out; idle input leaves data_out unchanged. When stalled both outputs hold. data_in_ready=(!new_data_out_valid)||data_out_ready is observed after the edge.",
      "test_expectations": "Fourteen independent saved cycles check modulo wrap, stalls, idle-valid clearing and reset flush. Check every data and valid/ready output after every rising edge, including defined invalid-cycle data. Preserve all saved expected values and 50 ns.",
